          "start_ms": null,
          "status": "machine-unreviewed",
          "text": "Description: On March 14, 2014 at 7:30 PM, a motorist and his daughter observed through the windshield the very fast movement of a luminous phenomenon in the cloudy sky. The phenomenon disappeared behind the horizon. The observation of a large, very bright point, followed by a short trail, crossing a portion of the sky in about 1 second, suggests a meteor (the very fast atmospheric entry of a meteorite, a small rocky body). This phenomenon was observed by numerous other witnesses who wrote about it on forums: Meteor of March 14, 2014. See also a video taken in Spanish Catalonia: Meteor in Spain. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"A\", identified as a meteor. See also: explanation: Meteor.",
          "translation_text_sha256": "093b4ead1792f65d4ae7b0162768b6ff40f233428080a690e9cecee50ab882d1"
        }
